A||N||9||jdbaker||Popeye Calf's||||8||
Z||000000||jdbaker||10-09-2001||10:15 PM||||Dear Forum Members:<P>The clutch pedal back pressure is so great on my '87 Mera I'm concerned that my left pant leg will not fit over my leg soon from the muscle mass developing in my calf from holding down the clutch at traffic lights.<P>Is this normal?  I'm not a small guy and this thing is really tough.  Is there any way to reduce the back pressure (or increase the size of my left pant leg)?<P>Thanks for your help!<P>J.D.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-09-2001||10:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jdbaker:<BR><B>Dear Forum Members:<P>The clutch pedal back pressure is so great on my '87 Mera I'm concerned that my left pant leg will not fit over my leg soon from the muscle mass developing in my calf from holding down the clutch at traffic lights.<P>Is this normal?  I'm not a small guy and this thing is really tough.  Is there any way to reduce the back pressure (or increase the size of my left pant leg)?<P>Thanks for your help!<P>J.D.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey JD!<BR>Sounds like you need to lube the clutch!<BR>Remove the inspection cover and while a friend holds the clutch down, spray lithium grease over everything in there!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>This is of course a JOKE!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Donno, could be a bad pressure plate, as that is what gives the return pressure you feel...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-10-2001||02:55 AM||||I know this much &lt;holding my thumb and first finger a millimeter apart&gt; about transmissions....sorry.<BR>But, dont "hold the clutch in at trafficlights"....causes premature wear on the clutch and pressure plate. I put it in neutral on my 4 speed while at lights. It must work to, my pants fit fine!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||10-10-2001||07:15 AM||||What My7Fieros said, but it most effects the throwout bearing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||10-10-2001||02:24 PM||||Dosent holding down the clutch for a long time make your foot fall asleep anyways?  Its better to just have to push in and let out the clutch a few more times to put it in gear and take it out than it is to hold it disengaged.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jdbaker||10-10-2001||07:02 PM||||Guys:<P>All good feedback on letting the clutch out while waiting for the light to change, and I have been doing that more, but I have two concerns with that approach.<P>1:  After sitting with the clutch out at a light, once the light changes, I have always worried about the load on the syncros in the transmission when you go from everything spinning to wanting to engage first gear.  Mine always needs to be "eased" in first to get everything to mesh nice.<P>2:  If you get rear ended while waiting at the light with clutch out, there's a good chance that the impact will disengage your foot from the break pedal and now you "sail" into the intersection or the car ahead of you with almost all of the energy delivered to you from the car that hit you (can that dump truck barreling through the intersection stop....?).<P>Anyway, it's just the stiffest clutch I've ever driven, but such is life.<P>J.D.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||10-10-2001||11:02 PM||||I do know from experience that getrag transmissions have a lot stiffer clutch than my isuzu or the muncie that I have driven, so it's not like yours is something completely unique.<P>Also, I just re-read your post, and noticed that your car is a Mera.  Have you registered your car with Rodney Dickman?  He is very interested in Mera's and has his own database of registered owners.  He could probably tell you everything about them.  go to his website at <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  and check it out.||||reg||3
Z||000007||SLYGUY||10-11-2001||01:29 PM||||What the hell is a "Mera"?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000008||onfire||10-11-2001||01:34 PM||||Go to the gym and work out the other leg. Then get bigger pants. lol <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||jdbaker||10-11-2001||07:31 PM||||Thanks to everyone for the feedback!<P>FieroJoe, I've already registered my Mera with Rodney.  As a matter of fact, he was a great resource as I looked to purchase a Mera.  I've now also begun diverting some of my income to his bank account in order to take advantage of some his outstanding products.<P>SlyGuy, here's a web site will give you the scoop on the Mera.  Check out:  <A HREF="http://fiero.net/mera/" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero.net/mera/</A> <P>J.D.||||reg||1
